  "text": {
    "intro": "Every maker presses in a different month, and each is privately certain the others have let theirs go to vinegar.\nFive makers are involved. Determine each maker's pressing month, apple and fault.\n- **Maker**: Araminta, Jethro, Morwenna, Petroc and Haskell.\n- **Pressing month** (listed from earlier to later): January, February, March, April and May.\n- **Apple**: Somerset Redstreak, Kingston Black, Browns Apple, Yarlington Mill and Foxwhelp.\n- **Fault**: ropiness, acetification, sulphur, a stuck ferment and mousiness.\nEvery maker has a different pressing month, apple and fault, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The maker who is accused of a stuck ferment presses in March.",
      "The maker who presses Kingston Black does not press in March. Morwenna and March are exactly two months apart in pressing month order.",
      "Jethro is exactly one month earlier than March, with no pressing month in between.",
      "The maker who presses Kingston Black does not press in January.",
      "The maker who presses Yarlington Mill is exactly one month earlier than Petroc, with no pressing month in between.",
      "Petroc is exactly one month earlier than the maker who presses Foxwhelp, with no pressing month in between.",
      "The maker who is accused of a stuck ferment is exactly one month earlier than the maker who presses Foxwhelp, with no pressing month in between.",
      "The maker who is accused of ropiness is exactly one month earlier than the maker who presses Somerset Redstreak, with no pressing month in between.",
      "The maker who is accused of mousiness and Haskell are exactly four months apart in pressing month order.",
      "The maker who is accused of sulphur and Haskell are exactly one month apart in pressing month order, in one direction or the other."
    ]
